<p>Israeli naval forces intercepted vessels from the Global Sumud Flotilla in international waters near Greece late Wednesday and early Thursday, flotilla organizers and Israeli media reports said, according to several publications. Organizers described the flotilla as a humanitarian mission carrying aid and activists to Gaza and said it set out to challenge Israel&#x27;s naval blockade of the territory. Reports gave differing figures as the operation developed: Al Jazeera said seven of 58 vessels had been captured near Crete, El País reported at least 15 boats boarded, including the mothership SAF SAF, and Independent Turkish cited organizers saying 21 boats had been detained while other vessels moved toward or entered Greek territorial waters. Dennik N, citing CTK, reported that about 175 people aboard more than 20 vessels were being taken to Israel. Israeli Army Radio cited an Israeli source as saying Israel had begun taking control of Gaza-bound aid ships far from its shores. Ynet reported that officials said the navy moved to enforce the Gaza maritime blockade against a convoy they described as about 100 vessels carrying about 1,000 activists. A separate Ynet item said an Israeli official attributed the decision to intercept the flotilla in international waters to its size.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/bbgaB7pewJYEoDdG8IcpDfzDhgmt4hDm3DCn0H7XMFnAoYC0sshlJHPkl2dTFEHHyxvR_LTjdASHxtMrNKqdGl6zjQtAgfgtf2tB_e2mcRFbmJ1ATPJRlZYRq6RD747tUTwUOfQ2PPQU59lo25TrhswMo_Lt2Bx0b8SBoKrBhF-hmkqXpDtWfbD6UAd1F8KQN2b43JKnfjFXOnRq4Y74dFK3fhCu01fftanQGXLGVUvZJvfQ8Nwvpir07w' alt='Boats carrying activists and humanitarian aid for Palestinians in Gaza reposition in the port during a symbolic send-off as part of the Global Sumud Flotilla, in Barcelona, Spain, Sunday, April 12, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Reported tactics: Organizers said Israeli speedboats approached while drones and warships were visible nearby, and activists said lasers and semi-automatic weapons were pointed at participants who were ordered to kneel.</li><li>Lost contact: The flotilla said it lost contact with 11 vessels before later reports put the number of boats without communication at 18.</li><li>Live documentation: El País said the flotilla issued SOS alerts and broadcast live images from the moment soldiers boarded decks.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Global Sumud Flotilla: Organizers described the boarding as an illegal seizure of civilian vessels in international waters and said no state has the right to control or occupy those waters. (<a href='https://minutemirror.com.pk/israel-seizes-gaza-aid-ships-in-international-waters-548166/'>Minute Mirror</a>)</li><li>Danny Danon, Israel&#x27;s ambassador to the UN: Danon said the vessels were stopped shortly before they entered an Israel-controlled zone and praised the navy&#x27;s action. (<a href='https://fakti.bg/world/1051465-izrael-spra-humanitarna-flotilia-za-gaza-v-mejdunarodni-vodi-krai-garcia'>Fakti.bg</a>)</li><li>Tariq Ra&#x27;ouf, activist aboard one vessel: Ra&#x27;ouf said Israeli military ships sent smaller boats to surround their vessel and broadcast music over communication channels, which he described as a psychological tactic. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330457653/israeli-forces-intercept-gaza-bound-aid-flotilla-in-mediterranean'>Aaj TV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/30/israel-seizes-global-sumud-flotilla-boats-1000km-away-from-gaza'>Israel seizes Global Sumud Flotilla boats 1,000km away from Gaza</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://novaramedia.com/2026/04/30/israel-illegally-intercepts-global-sumud-flotilla-500-nautical-miles-from-gaza/'>Israel Illegally Intercepts Global Sumud Flotilla – 500 Nautical Miles From Gaza</a> - novaramedia.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/30/gaza-freedom-flotilla-says-boats-surrounded-by-israeli-military_6752993_4.html'>Ga